  "_comment": "Waves 14-16 parallel track ownership. See ORDENCE-WAVE-PLAN-DELEGATION.md. A path belongs to exactly one track. `shared` is owned by integration only. `excludes` wins over `paths`: a broad glob minus the files lent to another track. SQL-FILES is owned by NUMBER BLOCK, not by directory: any track may add SQL-FILES/NNNN_*.sql when NNNN is inside its own block. Unnumbered files in SQL-FILES are ordinary owned paths: VERIFY and DRILL belong to C, the read-only checkers to H. `anyTrack` paths may be delivered by any track: drills are inert by name and belong with the work that needs them. `repairsInPlace` is an explicit, argued exception: an already-applied migration may be edited only when it aborts the sequence, so no later file can fix it. Wave 18 adds tracks I (Schema) and N (Core). H keeps 0166-0168, which it has already used for three tracks' unnumbered files, and holds 0181-0195 for later. I and N took 0169-0180. Wave 19 adds the migration tracks M1-M8. M2 owns server/import/**, which includes M7's dryrun.ts by glob, so M7's file is listed explicitly and M2 excludes it. Track I lends db/schema/import-runs.ts to M2, because the run ledger and its Drizzle definition are one decision and splitting them across two chats guarantees they disagree.",
